# Phaino Release Notes

## 0.1.1 (03 Nov 2026)

### New Features

- Initial release

## 0.1.2 (03 Nov 2026)

### Bug Fixes

- Fixed issues with directory status not changing when traversing within app

## 0.2.0 (04 Nov 2026)

### New Features

- Added go-to line command
- Added a formatter system that allows users to format certain file types with Phaino "best picks" of formatters (very opinionated)
- Added a tab for saving directories as "projects"
- Added features for keyboard driven navigation to allow the file tree in explorer to be more easily accessible via keyboard
- Added "session restore" which will always open the last directory the user had open on close

## 0.3.0 (05 Nov 2026)

### New Features

- Added a command palette (`Ctrl+Shift+P`) for quick access to any action in the app
- Added search and replace across files with per-file review, skipping files that have unsaved changes

### Improvements

- Moved breadcrumbs to the status bar to show the current file's path relative to the project root
- Replaced the Settings menu with a unified Preferences dialog consolidating theme, formatting, editor, and appearance settings
- Added a line wrapping toggle (`Alt+Z`) and a line numbers toggle (`Ctrl+Shift+L`)
- Added a trailing whitespace indicator that can be enabled in Preferences
- Added "Open in Terminal" to the Explorer context menu for quickly opening a shell in the selected folder
- Added a Recent files list (File → Recent) showing the last 10 opened files
- Added per-language toggles for format on save, configurable in Preferences
- Unified checkbox styling across the Search panel and Preferences dialog

### Bug Fixes

- Fixed the status bar Git indicator not reflecting the repository of the currently active file
- Fixed the file explorer not highlighting modified files until the first file modification event
- Fixed the Git panel not refreshing after commit, undo commit, push, or pull operations
- Fixed the line wrap toggle jumping the cursor to the end of the file
- Fixed the terminal Stop button being silently unusable when a process failed to start
- Fixed the save action silently skipping formatting when the file was open with unsaved changes

## 0.3.1 (05 Nov 2026)

### Bug Fixes

- Fixing issue in README with feature list entries not being on new lines
